cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FairFuzzKV-Codec: Tokenizer-Fragmentation-Aware KV-Cache Compression"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Badampudi"
    given-names: "Agasthya Anirudh"
    email: "anirudhbadampudi@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/akshat333-debug/FairFuzz-KV-Codec"
abstract: >-
  A memory-conscious codec for transformer Key-Value caches, with exact byte
  accounting, a versioned binary container format (FFK1), scalar INT8/INT4 and
  Linde-Buzo-Gray vector quantization, Golomb-Rice metadata coding, group-aware
  pruning with a local per-head attention-mass bound, and aggregate plus
  fairness-constrained minimax bit allocation. The project additionally tested,
  under four pre-registered gates, whether tokenizer fragmentation causes
  disproportionate compression damage to non-English text. Two of the four
  gates returned negative results and are reported as such: the fairness
  allocator showed no worst-cohort benefit (Gate 2, FAIL) and fuzzy
  repair-priority scoring did not beat no-repair (Gate 4, FAIL). The codec
  deliverable is independent of, and unaffected by, those negative findings.
keywords:
  - kv-cache-compression
  - vector-quantization
  - tokenizer-fairness
  - multilingual-nlp
  - reproducible-research
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-01"
